op at the blockhouse and Trail of Tears features, and keep the outing within posted park hours.","short_summary":"Combine a group hike with a respectful visit to Conway’s documented historic landscape.","evidence_claim":"Conway Parks lists Cadron Settlement Park as a public park with hiking trails, the blockhouse, Cherokee Trail of Tears attractions, and picnic sites.","source_url":"https://api.conwayarkansas.gov/parks/park-facilities/","source_title":"Parks & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"General park, trail, and historic-site access has no admission or purchase requirement listed; pavilion reservations are optional and separate.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"beaverfork-disc-golf-round","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Beaverfork Lake Park Disc Golf Course","title":"Play a Bring-Your-Own Disc Round","subtitle":"No-fee outdoor game at Beaverfork Lake Park","notes":"Bring discs you already own or borrow them from a friend, split into small groups, and keep clear of other park users.","short_summary":"Organize a casual disc-golf round using the public park course and shared gear.","evidence_claim":"Conway Parks lists a disc golf course among Beaverfork Lake Park’s public outdoor amenities, with no course admission or required purchase stated.","source_url":"https://api.conwayarkansas.gov/parks/park-facilities/","source_title":"Parks & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Course use has no admission or purchase requirement listed; bring or borrow discs so the activity remains zero-dollar.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"simon-park-conversation-hang","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Simon Park","title":"Hold a Downtown Conversation Circle","subtitle":"Public benches and bandstand space on Front Street","notes":"Gather at the benches for a conversation game or informal reading, keeping the bandstand clear if a reserved event is underway.","short_summary":"Use a named downtown park for an easy, no-purchase group catch-up.","evidence_claim":"Conway Parks identifies Simon Park as a public park with a covered bandstand, park benches, and a picnic table.","source_url":"https://api.conwayarkansas.gov/parks/park-facilities/","source_title":"Parks & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Casual public-park access requires no admission or purchase; reserving the bandstand is separate and not needed for a bench meetup.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
